{
  "dom_id": "step-q222046",
  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "What is the inverse of $f(x)=12{x}^{2}-35$ for $x\\ge 0?$\n\n${f}^{-1}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "To find the inverse of a function, we follow these steps:\n\n**Step 1:** Replace $f(x)$ with $y$:\n\n$$\ny=12{x}^{2}-35\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Swap $x$ and $y$:\n\n$$\nx=12{y}^{2}-35\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Solve for $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =12{y}^{2}-35 \\\\ x+35 & =12{y}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{x+35}{12} & ={y}^{2} \\\\ \\sqrt{\\frac{x+35}{12}} & =y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we selected the positive square root because if $x\\ge 0$ is the domain of $f,$ then the range of the inverse is ${f}^{-1}\\ge 0.$\n\n**Step 4:** Replace $y$ with ${f}^{-1}(x)$:\n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=\\sqrt{\\frac{x+35}{12}}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
